Z||000000||ounmongk||09-10-2000||06:27 PM||||Hi all, <BR>I've been away from the computer. Once my current motor( 87 SE 4-cyl) turns 100K miles, I'm going to put in a new header. I've thought about the Super Competition manifolds from Summit, but does anyone recommend anything else? How does this Ocelot system from the Fiero Store hold up? I've asked this question before, but I can't think for the life of me what the thread was called!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Oh, one more thing, I've heard that the fuel pressure can be "turned up" so to speak, on a Holly big-bore TBI. Presumably, the 87-88 has the larger TBI... so, I was wondering if the pressure could be "up-ped" a bit? A performance article I read says to increase it to 15 pounds.... hmm?<P>I can't wait to get my new motor so that I can soup that 'sucka' up!! <BR>Thanks everyone.||||reg||5
